`text_markdown_v2_urled` returns `_parse_markdown(self.text, self.parse_entities(), urled=True, version=2)`. In `_parse_markdown`, entities are sorted by offset and converted to Markdown inserts. The bold entity spans `"bold and italic"` and contains the italic entity, so the recursive nested-entity handling first turns the inner text into `_italic_`, then wraps the outer text as `*bold and _italic_*`. The URL entity with `urled=True` becomes a Markdown link whose visible text is `escaped_text`, and `escape_markdown(..., version=2)` escapes `.` and `_`, giving `http://example\.com/a\_b` as the label while keeping the target URL unescaped in parentheses. The code entity uses the code-specific branch, producing `` `x_y` ``, and the surrounding plain text segments are concatenated around those inserts.

## Answer
{"markdown_text":"start *bold and _italic_* end plus [http://example\\.com/a\\_b](http://example.com/a_b) and code `x_y`"}
